		<h1>About GridPermit</h1>
		<p>GridPermit is an independent educational platform built to help California homeowners understand residential solar energy and battery storage decisions.</p>

		<h2>Educational Purpose</h2>
		<p>GridPermit currently provides a simple, clearly-labeled illustrative system-size estimate based on standardized placeholder assumptions — not real utility rate data or property-specific analysis. We say so plainly on every page rather than implying more precision than the tool actually has; see our <a href="/methodology" style="color:#2563eb;">Methodology</a> for the exact numbers used. Our goal is to offer transparent informational tools, with optional links to independent third-party solar marketplaces.</p>

		<h2>Independent Referral Model</h2>
		<p>GridPermit is not a solar installer, contractor, engineering firm, public utility, or government agency. We do not provide engineering calculations or binding price quotes. When users click outbound links to request installer quotes, GridPermit may receive compensation from our affiliate marketplace partners at no additional cost to the user.</p>
